[4] Golden Farey spine
----------------------
On p/q=F_i/F_{i+1}, p+q is the next Fibonacci number.
p*q is the K_{p,q} incidence area; powers are order-stress tests.
F_2/F_3=1/2: p+q=3=F_4, p*q=2, sum_pairs=1, factor_pairs(product)=0, Zeck(p+q)=[3], power_winner=q^p
F_3/F_4=2/3: p+q=5=F_5, p*q=6, sum_pairs=2, factor_pairs(product)=1, Zeck(p+q)=[5], power_winner=q^p
F_4/F_5=3/5: p+q=8=F_6, p*q=15, sum_pairs=3, factor_pairs(product)=1, Zeck(p+q)=[8], power_winner=p^q
F_5/F_6=5/8: p+q=13=F_7, p*q=40, sum_pairs=6, factor_pairs(product)=3, Zeck(p+q)=[13], power_winner=p^q
F_6/F_7=8/13: p+q=21=F_8, p*q=104, sum_pairs=10, factor_pairs(product)=3, Zeck(p+q)=[21], power_winner=p^q
F_7/F_8=13/21: p+q=34=F_9, p*q=273, sum_pairs=16, factor_pairs(product)=3, Zeck(p+q)=[34], power_winner=p^q
