[6] Tournament Analysis
-----------------------
vertices: proof currencies / representation fibers, not runners
pairwise observable: coordinate-wise retention vector
switch/gauge: majority of better-retained proof coordinates
tie Hamiltonian path: exact_farey_packet > summand_antidiagonal_fiber > multiplicand_hyperbola_fiber > zeckendorf_path_carry > fibonacci_pascal_row > fermat_polygonal_invoice > ternary_goldbach_smoothing > binary_goldbach_pair_sieve > farey_power_stress
exact_farey_packet                 score=8 vector=(5, 4, 4, 4, 3, 3, 4, 5, 5)
  preserves: p/q, q, Farey excess, route labels
  destroys: nothing intentional; this is the base packet
summand_antidiagonal_fiber         score=7 vector=(4, 5, 2, 3, 3, 4, 3, 4, 4)
  preserves: additive lane, pinch denominators, Pascal rows
  destroys: factor sparsity, ordered magnitude
multiplicand_hyperbola_fiber       score=6 vector=(4, 2, 5, 2, 2, 2, 4, 4, 4)
  preserves: product lane, Kpq incidence, factor fibers
  destroys: additive branch multiplicity, carry order
zeckendorf_path_carry              score=5 vector=(3, 4, 2, 5, 3, 1, 3, 4, 5)
  preserves: canonical support, path conflict graph, carry confluence
  destroys: representation abundance, prime residue smoothing
fibonacci_pascal_row               score=4 vector=(3, 5, 1, 4, 3, 2, 2, 3, 4)
  preserves: row fiber, path independent-set ranks, carry width
  destroys: chosen normal form, multiplicative incidence
fermat_polygonal_invoice           score=3 vector=(2, 4, 1, 2, 5, 2, 4, 3, 4)
  preserves: finite summand budget, side-count invoice, local residues
  destroys: uniqueness, prime smoothing entropy
ternary_goldbach_smoothing         score=2 vector=(2, 4, 1, 1, 2, 5, 5, 2, 3)
  preserves: many branches, local residue rank, circle-method shape
  destroys: canonical support, bounded deterministic invoice
binary_goldbach_pair_sieve         score=1 vector=(2, 4, 1, 1, 1, 4, 5, 2, 3)
  preserves: pair graph, singular series hints, prime residue channels
  destroys: third-variable smoothing, normal form
farey_power_stress                 score=0 vector=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 5)
  preserves: magnitude flip detector
  destroys: proof scale, fiber identity, safe quotient data
score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1, 7: 1, 8: 1}
directed_3cycles=0
scc_sizes=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
hamiltonian_path_count=1

[7] Merged packet rule
----------------------
A representation/Farey quotient is theorem-safe only after declaring:
  root Farey packet: p/q, q, excess, route labels
  summand shadow: p+q as antidiagonal fiber and additive/pinch row
  multiplicand shadow: p*q as factor/Kpq incidence fiber
  carry law: Pascal row and Zeckendorf no-adjacent normal form when used
  proof economy: smoothing, bounded arity, normal form, product incidence, or stress test
If one of those coordinates is forgotten, it must be reconstructed,
dual-annihilated, exact/coboundary, descended, or routed to a named residual.
